# J30 — verify:finding model-ladder options are discoverable and stored (P1)
#
# Keyless, deterministic. Enters the offline demo fixture (KUZUSHI_DEVEX_PHASE_
# FIXTURE), leaves Run Focus with `b`, then audits the verify:finding option
# surface: the P1 gateModel/escalationModel knobs are `.advanced()`, so Standard
# hides them and `show advanced` reveals them; a stored value sorts first; a
# malformed spec is accepted at setg (single-owner validation) but rejected
# legibly at dispatch. Ends with a non-TTY plain-parity probe of the same rows.
#
# macOS-keychain caveat: env-unset cannot mask OAuth-cached creds; this journey
# needs none — every step here is keyless.
name: verify:finding model-ladder options are discoverable and stored
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 KUZUSHI_DEVEX_PHASE_FIXTURE=1
launch:
wait-for: 25 CHOOSE A TARGET
submit: demo
# The settled fixture lands foreground in Run Focus (which owns input); leave it
# with `b`, then wait on the persistent findings-ledger footer to confirm the
# workbench origin is restored before submitting verbs.
wait-for: 120 RUN FOCUS
keys: b
wait-for: 30 findings / 1 crit
wait: 2
submit: options verify:finding
wait: 2
snap: options-standard
expect: verify:finding
expect-not: gateModel
expect-not: escalationModel
submit: show advanced
wait: 2
snap: options-advanced
expect: gateModel
expect: escalationModel
expect: provider:modelId
ask: Advanced rows — can an operator tell from the description alone what the gate trusts (rejection only) and that escalation fires only on a split? No docs allowed.
submit: setg gateModel openai:gpt-cheap
wait: 1
submit: setg escalationModel openai:gpt-strong
wait: 1
# gateModel/escalationModel are advanced rows, so the stored value is only shown
# under the advanced filter — a fresh `options` reopens in Standard.
submit: options verify:finding
wait: 1
submit: show advanced
wait: 2
snap: options-stored-first
# The advanced view lists gateModel/escalationModel FIRST, each with a stored
# openai: value (the value column truncates the full id; the full id is shown
# in the Prove MODEL LADDER card, J31).
expect: gateModel
expect: escalationModel
expect: openai:
ask: Stored rows sort first — does the stored value read as "this WILL apply to the next verify", with global-vs-session scope legible? (Full model id is legible in the Prove card, J31.)
# malformed spec: accepted at setg (single-owner validation), must fail legibly at dispatch
submit: setg gateModel nonsense
wait: 1
submit: run verify:finding {"fingerprint":"escalated-split-fixture"}
wait-snap: 20 not a valid model spec | malformed-dispatch-error
expect: gateModel
expect: not a valid model spec
ask: The error names the option AND the expected provider:modelId shape — is the fix obvious from the message, given setg accepted the bad value silently?
ask: gateModel/escalationModel are Prove-time verify knobs, not Setup readiness rows — nothing in Setup implies gateModel gates Start Map (L24).
# Dismiss the failed-run receipt notice, then exit with Ctrl+C (idle exit) —
# robust across the post-run transitional view where a typed `quit` draft races.
keys: Escape
wait: 2
keys: C-c
wait: 3
launch-raw: printf 'options verify:finding\nshow advanced\nquit\n' | @KUZUSHI --target @TMP_TARGET --no-session-persistence 2>&1 | head -60
wait: 6
snap: plain-options
# Plain narrows the name column (escalationModel -> "escalationM..."); assert the
# rows are present by their legible prefix.
expect: gateModel
expect: escalation
ask: Same rows, same descriptions, no ANSI, no box-drawing dependency?
